-Oh boy.

1055
00:45:19,952 --> 00:45:23,155
-Oh, let's see, he who
reads these words of wit

1056
00:45:23,188 --> 00:45:24,155
eats his little balls.

1057
00:45:24,188 --> 00:45:28,060
Oh, now that's immature
even for the Dark Ages.

1058
00:45:28,093 --> 00:45:30,462
-For a good time, call Dong.

1059
00:45:30,495 --> 00:45:31,230
-Thong.

1060
00:45:31,263 --> 00:45:33,598
-Thong.

1061
00:45:33,632 --> 00:45:34,232
-Huh?

1062
00:45:38,337 --> 00:45:40,438
-They're kind of dumb,
they're easy to kill.

1063
00:45:40,472 --> 00:45:41,840
The American Gladiators!

1064
00:45:49,313 --> 00:45:51,917
-Ah, something dull.

1065
00:45:51,950 --> 00:45:53,918
Come towards it, our friend.

1066
00:45:53,952 --> 00:45:56,388
-By the stubbing of
my thumb, something

1067
00:45:56,422 --> 00:45:59,925
stupid this way comes.

1068
00:45:59,958 --> 00:46:01,560
-Uh-huh, just as I thought.

1069
00:46:01,593 --> 00:46:03,228
-Checks out.

1070
00:46:03,262 --> 00:46:04,195
-Meter man.

1071
00:46:07,032 --> 00:46:08,000
-Knock it off up there!

1072
00:46:12,003 --> 00:46:15,040
-For a good time,
call-- stupid rock.

1073
00:46:15,073 --> 00:46:18,210
Stupid, stupid rock.

1074
00:46:18,243 --> 00:46:19,578
-Oh, man.

1075
00:46:19,612 --> 00:46:21,112
-Find a way out?

1076
00:46:21,147 --> 00:46:22,180
-Stupid rock.

1077
00:46:22,213 --> 00:46:23,148
-Good thing you
were here, Gomez,

1078
00:46:23,182 --> 00:46:25,217
we would have never
found it without you.

1079
00:46:28,587 --> 00:46:29,822
-Huh?

1080
00:46:29,855 --> 00:46:32,723
-Dreezle drazzle drozzle drome,
time for zis one to come home.

1081
00:46:32,757 --> 00:46:35,193
-So Bob Hope owns all of that?

1082
00:46:35,227 --> 00:46:38,963
-Yeah, yeah, we're thinking of
turning it into a nine holer.

1083
00:46:38,997 --> 00:46:41,065
-You have failed, Sandor.

1084
00:46:41,098 --> 00:46:42,700
-Bad country singer, bad Willie.

1085
00:46:42,733 --> 00:46:44,402
---precious time!

1086
00:46:44,435 --> 00:46:46,137
If you had all
the magical powers

1087
00:46:46,172 --> 00:46:47,438
that you told me you had--

1088
00:46:47,472 --> 00:46:49,608
-Again with the finger!

1089
00:46:49,642 --> 00:46:51,743
-I don't see how I failed.

1090
00:46:51,777 --> 00:46:53,678
-You don't, eh?

1091
00:46:53,712 --> 00:46:55,547
Well, you soon will.

1092
00:46:55,580 --> 00:46:57,382
Guards!

1093
00:46:57,415 --> 00:46:59,150
-Hey, Paul Wellstone.

1094
00:46:59,183 --> 00:47:05,090
-If after all this time Sandor
has been worthy of your esteem,

1095
00:47:05,123 --> 00:47:09,795
then you are as guilty of
having failed as he is.

1096
00:47:09,828 --> 00:47:11,330
-Flog him!

1097
00:47:11,363 --> 00:47:13,065
-Thank you, sir.

1098
00:47:13,098 --> 00:47:14,065
-Please, have mercy.

1099
00:47:14,098 --> 00:47:17,568
-I fear for you, Sandor.

1100
00:47:17,602 --> 00:47:20,072
Mercy does not dwell
in the hearts of those

1101
00:47:20,105 --> 00:47:23,275
without spiritual
strength and wisdom.

1102
00:47:23,308 --> 00:47:26,245
-Oh, bite me, it's fun!

1103
00:47:26,278 --> 00:47:28,213
-Very well.

1104
00:47:28,247 --> 00:47:29,213
Imprison him.

1105
00:47:29,247 --> 00:47:32,150
I'll employ some tricks
of my own against Ator,

1106
00:47:32,183 --> 00:47:34,553
and you can use your time to
come up with something new,

1107
00:47:34,587 --> 00:47:36,455
and it better be
good, Sandor, if you

1108
00:47:36,488 --> 00:47:39,157
want to regain my esteem.

1109
00:47:39,190 --> 00:47:44,563
And I think you know how
important for you is my esteem.

1110
00:47:44,597 --> 00:47:47,165
-OK, OK, I'll do linking
rings, I'll do ball in the cup,

1111
00:47:47,198 --> 00:47:48,700
I'll do metamorphosis,
wait, wait!

1112
00:47:53,838 --> 00:47:55,240
-I'm scared.

1113
00:47:55,273 --> 00:47:57,375
Oh, we're already there.

1114
00:47:57,408 --> 00:47:58,743
-It's much too quite here.

1115
00:47:58,777 --> 00:48:00,445
-Too too quiet.

1116
00:48:00,478 --> 00:48:01,680
-Not a good sign.

1117
00:48:01,713 --> 00:48:03,782
-I sense the presence
of something evil.

1118
00:48:03,815 --> 00:48:04,415
-That's you.

1119
00:48:04,448 --> 00:48:07,485
-Zor must be at work here.

1120
00:48:07,518 --> 00:48:10,122
-Since we left the
caves, I've had

1121
00:48:10,155 --> 00:48:11,523
the feeling that
we're being followed.

1122
00:48:11,557 --> 00:48:13,558
-Uh, that's me, boss,
I'm right behind you.

1123
00:48:16,462 --> 00:48:18,463
-I don't know, but
we'll soon find out.

1124
00:48:25,770 --> 00:48:26,838
-Quick, hide.

1125
00:48:26,872 --> 00:48:29,540
-Oh no, they've jumped right
in into a Kurosawa film.

1126
00:48:33,845 --> 00:48:35,213
-So it'll start making sense?

1127
00:48:35,247 --> 00:48:35,647
-Mmhmm.

1128
00:48:40,185 --> 00:48:42,487
-Toshiro Mifune, right there

1129
00:48:42,520 --> 00:48:44,288
-I'm huge!

1130
00:48:44,322 --> 00:48:45,890
Dig me.

1131
00:48:45,923 --> 00:48:48,427
-Yeah.

1132
00:48:48,460 --> 00:48:49,460
-Oh no, a mime.

1133
00:48:56,233 --> 00:48:57,568
-Did he mention he's huge?

1134
00:48:57,602 --> 00:49:01,340
He does that.

1135
00:49:01,373 --> 00:49:03,742
-Warriors, come out and play!

1136
00:49:07,645 --> 00:49:09,413
-No, you see, I used two blades.

1137
00:49:09,447 --> 00:49:11,883
The first blade lifts the
head away from the body

1138
00:49:11,917 --> 00:49:14,452
before the head can snap back.

1139
00:49:14,485 --> 00:49:18,490
And then, bluh-- below
the skin level, yeah.

1140
00:49:18,523 --> 00:49:19,858
-We get it.

1141
00:49:23,295 --> 00:49:25,897
-Come on, come on!

1142
00:49:25,930 --> 00:49:27,865
-Ooh, right in the bread basket.

1143
00:49:32,603 --> 00:49:34,038
-You know, the reason
this scene is so good

1144
00:49:34,072 --> 00:49:36,408
is because we care
about the characters.

1145
00:49:36,442 --> 00:49:39,510
-We do.

1146
00:49:39,543 --> 00:49:40,745
-I mean, we do?

1147
00:49:40,778 --> 00:49:41,847
-We really do.

1148
00:49:45,517 --> 00:49:46,785
-Hey, it's the
life of the party,

1149
00:49:46,818 --> 00:49:48,953
he's got a lampshade
on his head.

1150
00:49:48,987 --> 00:49:50,788
-He'll be the death
of the party, soon.

1151
00:49:57,428 --> 00:49:59,397
-Wicker armor,
courtesy Pier One.

1152
00:49:59,430 --> 00:50:00,832
Doesn't work too well,
it's just decorative.

1153
00:50:00,865 --> 00:50:01,933
-Hurts, don't it?

1154
00:50:05,103 --> 00:50:09,040
-Look out, its
Koko the Terrible!

1155
00:50:09,073 --> 00:50:10,942
[LAUGHS] Goofy old mime.

1156
00:50:14,512 --> 00:50:15,847
-Oops.

1157
00:50:15,880 --> 00:50:16,482
Ouch.

1158
00:50:20,585 --> 00:50:23,422
-OK, just like we rehearsed it.

1159
00:50:23,455 --> 00:50:25,690
Over, cross, ha ha!

1160
00:50:25,723 --> 00:50:27,025
I will kill you!

1161
00:50:29,862 --> 00:50:30,428
-Oh.

1162
00:50:30,462 --> 00:50:33,098
-Or not.

1163
00:50:33,132 --> 00:50:35,833
-Hey, is this where
the kegger is?

1164
00:50:35,867 --> 00:50:37,902
We stalled Mark's van in front.

1165
00:50:37,935 --> 00:50:39,037
-No, wait.

1166
00:50:39,070 --> 00:50:41,005
-Uh, we just remembered,
uh, we didn't

1167
00:50:41,038 --> 00:50:42,073
leave enough change
in the meter.

1168
00:50:42,107 --> 00:50:42,807
We're double parked!

1169
00:50:42,840 --> 00:50:43,975
Bye!

1170
00:50:44,008 --> 00:50:45,110
-No use chasing them.

1171
00:50:45,143 --> 00:50:46,712
Save your strength.

1172
00:50:46,745 --> 00:50:49,080
The castle of the Great
One is still far away.

1173
00:50:49,113 --> 00:50:50,882
-And the end of the
movie is even further.

1174
00:50:50,915 --> 00:50:52,683
-Well said.

1175
00:50:52,717 --> 00:50:53,452
-What I mean is--

1176
00:50:53,485 --> 00:50:54,618
-Hey, [INAUDIBLE].

1177
00:50:54,652 --> 00:50:55,753
---certain risk
involved for you.

1178
00:50:55,787 --> 00:51:01,460
In stopping Ator, I might,
inadvertently, of course,

1179
00:51:01,493 --> 00:51:03,462
also harm your daughter.

1180
00:51:03,495 --> 00:51:04,595
What do you say to that?

1181
00:51:04,628 --> 00:51:07,098
-I say you could drive a
Mack truck through your cues.

1182
00:51:07,132 --> 00:51:08,633
Tempo, tempo, pick it up!

1183
00:51:08,667 --> 00:51:11,470
-I must admit,
that as a murderer,

1184
00:51:11,503 --> 00:51:15,207
you are most impressive.

1185
00:51:15,240 --> 00:51:19,643
-But as an Andrew
McCarthy fan, whoo!

1186
00:51:19,677 --> 00:51:24,883
-You will receive
nothing from me but pity.

1187
00:51:24,917 --> 00:51:26,585
-Careful, old man.

1188
00:51:26,618 --> 00:51:27,885
-Go to bed, old man!

1189
00:51:27,918 --> 00:51:29,587
-My patience has its limits.

1190
00:51:29,620 --> 00:51:30,622
-I'm aware of that fact.

1191
00:51:30,655 --> 00:51:31,557
-As does your talent.

1192
00:51:31,590 --> 00:51:35,027
-But I mustn't expect
too much from you.

1193
00:51:35,060 --> 00:51:37,128
Patience, after all,
is a virtue which

1194
00:51:37,162 --> 00:51:39,965
is found only in the strong.

1195
00:51:43,235 --> 00:51:44,502
-You're wonderful.

1196
00:51:44,535 --> 00:51:45,070
-Marry me.

1197
00:51:45,103 --> 00:51:47,172
-You do amuse me.

1198
00:51:47,205 --> 00:51:48,707
And provoke me.

1199
00:51:48,740 --> 00:51:51,142
-That is love, isn't it?

1200
00:51:51,175 --> 00:51:52,277
-What is it?

1201
00:51:52,310 --> 00:51:53,912
-Ator has escaped again.

1202
00:51:53,945 --> 00:51:54,545
-D'oh!

1203
00:51:57,248 --> 00:51:58,950
-Hi, Curt Gowdy here.

1204
00:51:58,983 --> 00:52:01,920
Join Thong and Phil Harris
and me out on the Idaho River,

1205
00:52:01,953 --> 00:52:03,888
fishing for trout.

1206
00:52:03,922 --> 00:52:07,292
-[LAUGHS] Now try
catching a steak, Dong.

1207
00:52:07,325 --> 00:52:07,958
-Thong.

1208
00:52:07,992 --> 00:52:08,593
-Thong.

1209
00:52:13,598 --> 00:52:14,732
-Ator, what's your dream?

1210
00:52:20,772 --> 00:52:21,640
-How big is God?

1211
00:52:24,808 --> 00:52:27,145
-For a moment back
there, I had the feeling

1212
00:52:27,178 --> 00:52:28,647
you knew those men
that attacked us.

1213
00:52:28,680 --> 00:52:29,280
Did you?

1214
00:52:29,313 --> 00:52:30,315
-Yes.

1215
00:52:30,348 --> 00:52:32,083
-Well, we played
varsity together.

1216
00:52:32,117 --> 00:52:33,618
-I do.

1217
00:52:33,652 --> 00:52:35,087
-Who were they?

1218
00:52:35,120 --> 00:52:39,057
-They're the survivors of
the noble tribe of Han.

1219
00:52:39,090 --> 00:52:43,160
They worship the
god of war, Soko.

1220
00:52:43,195 --> 00:52:44,395
-Soko?

1221
00:52:44,428 --> 00:52:46,698
I know that name.

1222
00:52:46,732 --> 00:52:48,233
-Oh, he dated my friend Sharon.

1223
00:52:48,267 --> 00:52:51,202
---the northern territory.

1224
00:52:51,235 --> 00:52:52,637
-Uh, what's Miles sitting on?

1225
00:52:52,670 --> 00:52:54,138
-His second in command
was his brother--

1226
00:52:54,172 --> 00:52:55,407
-I don't wanna know.

1227
00:52:55,440 --> 00:52:57,775
-In a great battle
against the Han,

1228
00:52:57,808 --> 00:53:00,045
Zor exterminated them,
but spared the lives

1229
00:53:00,078 --> 00:53:02,147
of three samurai,
and then used them

1230
00:53:02,180 --> 00:53:05,250
to kill his own brother
to usurp his power.

1231
00:53:05,283 --> 00:53:07,052
-Oh, if this is
another flashback,

1232
00:53:07,085 --> 00:53:08,487
I gotta go get a sandwich.

1233
00:53:08,520 --> 00:53:10,088
-Do you think that Zor will--

1234
00:53:10,122 --> 00:53:11,422
-It's OK.

1235
00:53:11,455 --> 00:53:13,758
-Do you think my
Father's still alive?

1236
00:53:13,792 --> 00:53:16,260
-Oh, sure. [SNORT LAUGHS]

1237
00:53:16,293 --> 00:53:19,197
-Zor wants to possess your
Father's knowledge, Mila.

1238
00:53:19,230 --> 00:53:21,465
-And your mother's wardrobe.

1239
00:53:21,498 --> 00:53:22,433
-And the geometric nucleus.

1240
00:53:25,937 --> 00:53:32,443
No, your father's safe
as long as he has it.

1241
00:53:32,477 --> 00:53:36,447
-Uh, that's enough fish, Dong,
thank you, thank you very much,

1242
00:53:36,480 --> 00:53:37,282
Dong, that's enough fish.

1243
00:53:37,315 --> 00:53:39,883
-Just a few dozen more.

1244
00:53:39,918 --> 00:53:42,920
-Why did you go and
live so far away?

1245
00:53:42,953 --> 00:53:43,922
-Well, it's on the bus line.

1246
00:53:43,955 --> 00:53:46,725
-Your father taught me
the path I must follow.

1247
00:53:46,758 --> 00:53:52,497
It is for this I
live the way I do.

1248
00:53:52,530 --> 00:53:55,067
-But shouldn't a man's destiny--

1249
00:53:55,100 --> 00:53:57,002
-Oh, I thought you were
going to say something else.

1250
00:53:57,035 --> 00:53:58,437
---coincide with the
desires of his heart?

1251
00:53:58,470 --> 00:54:01,005
-A man's destiny is
always predetermined--

1252
00:54:01,038 --> 00:54:01,873
-Oh, he's a Calvinist.

1253
00:54:01,907 --> 00:54:04,408
---by the true
desires of his heart.

1254
00:54:04,442 --> 00:54:09,013
I know what mine is, and I must
follow the lonely [INAUDIBLE].

1255
00:54:09,047 --> 00:54:12,350
-I'm sorry, I
didn't mean to pry.

1256
00:54:12,383 --> 00:54:15,320
-That's all right,
I'm glad you asked.

1257
00:54:15,353 --> 00:54:18,022
-What's your major?

1258
00:54:18,055 --> 00:54:19,023
-Thong?

1259
00:54:19,057 --> 00:54:20,125
The fish is ready.

1260
00:54:23,562 --> 00:54:26,030
-Oh, wow, what I wouldn't give
for a Weed Eater right now.

1261
00:54:33,905 --> 00:54:36,340
-Oh no, don't kill us!

1262
00:54:36,373 --> 00:54:39,043
-Uh, what will you give me?

1263
00:54:39,077 --> 00:54:40,378
-OK, you talked me into it.

1264
00:54:40,412 --> 00:54:41,012
-Huh?
What?

1265
00:54:41,045 --> 00:54:41,412
Mom?

1266
00:54:41,445 --> 00:54:42,047
Dad?

1267
00:54:42,080 --> 00:54:42,447
Uncle Dave?

1268
00:54:42,480 --> 00:54:43,080
Oh.

1269
00:54:48,887 --> 00:54:49,253
-Mila.

1270
00:54:49,287 --> 00:54:50,088
-What is it?

1271
00:54:50,122 --> 00:54:50,955
-Someone's coming.

1272
00:54:50,988 --> 00:54:52,190
Look.

1273
00:54:52,223 --> 00:54:52,923
-Cover your hip.

1274
00:54:52,957 --> 00:54:55,093
-Get dressed.

1275
00:54:55,127 --> 00:54:56,127
-Who are you?

1276
00:54:56,160 --> 00:54:57,995
-Uh, we're pirates.

1277
00:54:58,028 --> 00:54:59,263
-What do you want?

1278
00:54:59,297 --> 00:55:00,498
-Look, you captured us.

1279
00:55:03,267 --> 00:55:05,470
-[CLEARS THROAT] Line?

1280
00:55:05,503 --> 00:55:06,503
-Where do you come from?

1281
00:55:06,537 --> 00:55:07,905
-Everywhere and nowhere.

1282
00:55:11,242 --> 00:55:13,010
-Somebody say something.

1283
00:55:13,043 --> 00:55:15,413
-Well, answer.

1284
00:55:15,447 --> 00:55:17,248
Can't you speak?

1285
00:55:17,282 --> 00:55:18,248
-We're from Sulajin.

1286
00:55:18,282 --> 00:55:19,350
-Ehhn, wrong answer.

1287
00:55:19,383 --> 00:55:20,185
But thanks for playing.

1288
00:55:20,218 --> 00:55:21,218
Sulajin?

1289
00:55:23,320 --> 00:55:25,123
-Yes, it's to the north,
not far from here.

1290
00:55:25,157 --> 00:55:26,390
-Yeah, I worked out there.

1291
00:55:26,423 --> 00:55:28,693
-I know.

1292
00:55:28,727 --> 00:55:31,195
It's where my parents were born.

1293
00:55:31,228 --> 00:55:33,632
-Then you're Ator?

1294
00:55:33,665 --> 00:55:35,267
Pupil of the Great Master?

1295
00:55:35,300 --> 00:55:35,967
-Yeah, that's me.

1296
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:36,835
Pretty much.

1297
00:55:36,868 --> 00:55:38,703
-You may speak
without fear with me.

1298
00:55:38,737 --> 00:55:41,338
-Much evil has fallen on
the people of our village.

1299
00:55:41,372 --> 00:55:42,340
-Bummer.

1300
00:55:42,373 --> 00:55:44,375
-In order to survive,
we must make an offering

1301
00:55:44,408 --> 00:55:46,443
to be god of the Kungs.

1302
00:55:46,477 --> 00:55:49,580
Humans sacrificed to the
serpent god on every full moon.

1303
00:55:49,613 --> 00:55:51,382
-Besides, our people
are not warriors.

1304
00:55:51,415 --> 00:55:54,118
We're only poor farmers.

1305
00:55:54,152 --> 00:55:57,122
-If we don't get help
soon, we'll all die.

1306
00:55:57,155 --> 00:55:57,822
-Hmm, I like it.

1307
00:55:57,855 --> 00:55:59,423
Make it shorter, I'll buy it.

1308
00:55:59,457 --> 00:56:02,493
-The Kungs have always
demanded the blood of man.

1309
00:56:02,527 --> 00:56:04,295
-Ha, yeah, they're
funny that way.

1310
00:56:04,328 --> 00:56:06,063
-They'll soon finish you.

1311
00:56:06,097 --> 00:56:09,067
We must act quickly.

1312
00:56:09,100 --> 00:56:10,202
-But not right now.

1313
00:56:10,235 --> 00:56:12,203
In a minute or two.

1314
00:56:12,237 --> 00:56:13,170
Half an hour, maybe.

1315
00:56:13,203 --> 00:56:15,340
-Wow, check out the way
that guy moves, huh?

1316
00:56:15,373 --> 00:56:18,208
-What do you intend to do, Ator?

1317
00:56:18,242 --> 00:56:19,410
-We'll take them
back to the village,

1318
00:56:19,443 --> 00:56:21,045
and I'll speak
with their people.

1319
00:56:21,078 --> 00:56:23,313
-The Village People?

1320
00:56:23,347 --> 00:56:27,218
-The Kungs will kill us.

1321
00:56:27,252 --> 00:56:29,987
-I think-- we should run!

1322
00:56:30,020 --> 00:56:30,655
-Ah!

1323
00:56:30,688 --> 00:56:31,188
-No.

1324
00:56:31,222 --> 00:56:32,723
Let them go, Thong.

1325
00:56:32,757 --> 00:56:35,460
-If you love
something, let it go.

1326
00:56:35,493 --> 00:56:38,162
-We'll go without them.

1327
00:56:38,195 --> 00:56:39,197
-We'll hurry down there.

1328
00:56:39,230 --> 00:56:40,532
---first to volunteer?

1329
00:56:45,203 --> 00:56:47,472
-I'll be doing the death scene
from "Camille", thank you.

1330
00:56:50,408 --> 00:56:52,343
-And the next?

1331
00:56:52,377 --> 00:56:56,280
-Come forward, Cowardly Lion!

1332
00:56:56,313 --> 00:56:57,248
Oh, it's a woman.

1333
00:57:01,718 --> 00:57:04,188
-I could use a man like you.

1334
00:57:04,222 --> 00:57:05,490
And I do mean use.

1335
00:57:09,260 --> 00:57:12,430
-Uh, you, uh, never mind.

1336
00:57:12,463 --> 00:57:13,297
-Nice try.

1337
00:57:17,302 --> 00:57:18,803
-We need another.

1338
00:57:18,837 --> 00:57:20,538
-I'll go.

1339
00:57:20,572 --> 00:57:23,273
-Uh, no, you went last
time, one to a customer.

1340
00:57:23,307 --> 00:57:24,342
---not you my dear.

1341
00:57:24,375 --> 00:57:26,878
Our family's already given
one life to the Kungs.

1342
00:57:26,912 --> 00:57:30,715
-I must, or else another
will have to take my place.

1343
00:57:30,748 --> 00:57:34,418
-Nancy Walker in a cameo role.

1344
00:57:34,452 --> 00:57:34,818
-Wait!

1345
00:57:34,852 --> 00:57:35,953
-Hey!

1346
00:57:35,987 --> 00:57:39,190
It's speedy delivery guy,
and has he got a package!

1347
00:57:41,725 --> 00:57:42,593
-Stop!

1348
00:57:42,627 --> 00:57:43,495
-In the name of love.

1349
00:57:46,932 --> 00:57:48,465
-Just wait for me, I'll
be down in a minute.

1350
00:57:48,500 --> 00:57:51,268
Just stand there, I'm coming.

1351
00:57:51,302 --> 00:57:53,538
OK, well now-- oh.

1352
00:57:53,572 --> 00:57:56,540
I thought this was the
Anderson party, sorry.

1353
00:57:56,573 --> 00:57:59,210
I'll just be on my way.

1354
00:57:59,243 --> 00:58:01,578
-Who is this gentle
stranger with pecs

1355
00:58:01,612 --> 00:58:04,782
like melons and knees of fringe?

1356
00:58:04,815 --> 00:58:06,550
-Ator.

1357
00:58:06,583 --> 00:58:08,418
You have chosen
a day of mourning

1358
00:58:08,452 --> 00:58:10,222
to visit the village
of your parents.

1359
00:58:10,255 --> 00:58:10,955
-Afternoon.

1360
00:58:10,988 --> 00:58:14,492
-I've come to help you fight.

1361
00:58:14,525 --> 00:58:15,727
-We're not fighting them.

1362
00:58:15,760 --> 00:58:16,660
The Kungs will massacre us.

1363
00:58:16,693 --> 00:58:18,663
-You must.

1364
00:58:18,697 --> 00:58:21,665
If you go on like this, none
of you will be left alive.

1365
00:58:21,698 --> 00:58:23,267
-Dude looks like a lady.

1366
00:58:23,300 --> 00:58:24,235
[Stupid laughter]

1367
00:58:27,838 --> 00:58:29,007
-Where's Ravani?

1368
00:58:29,040 --> 00:58:29,540
-Who?

1369
00:58:29,573 --> 00:58:30,508
-Ravani has left us.

1370
00:58:30,542 --> 00:58:32,710
-Because he had nothing
to do with the film.

1371
00:58:32,743 --> 00:58:34,545
-He was too old to guide us.

1372
00:58:34,578 --> 00:58:36,847
-I have taken his
place as the elder.

1373
00:58:36,882 --> 00:58:39,417
-He was a proud, courageous man.

1374
00:58:39,450 --> 00:58:40,618
-But dumber than
a bag of hammers.

1375
00:58:43,353 --> 00:58:46,457
-He never would have allowed
such submissive behavior.

1376
00:58:46,490 --> 00:58:48,760
-What, are you
calling me a wussy?

1377
00:58:48,793 --> 00:58:50,428
-You must not lose heart.

1378
00:58:50,462 --> 00:58:51,095
I see great courage--

1379
00:58:51,128 --> 00:58:52,297
-Because a guy will eat it.

1380
00:58:52,330 --> 00:58:54,865
-Most of your young people
willingly sacrifice themselves

1381
00:58:54,898 --> 00:58:55,567
to be victims--

1382
00:58:55,600 --> 00:58:56,902
-Coffee.

1383
00:58:56,935 --> 00:58:57,835
Tea.

1384
00:58:57,868 --> 00:58:59,403
[INAUDIBLE] nuts.

1385
00:58:59,437 --> 00:59:00,738
---and fight back?

1386
00:59:00,772 --> 00:59:01,638
-Soft drinks.

1387
00:59:01,672 --> 00:59:02,740
---and I will help you!

1388
00:59:02,773 --> 00:59:03,942
You will regain your freedom--

1389
00:59:03,975 --> 00:59:04,375
-Juice?

1390
00:59:04,408 --> 00:59:06,510
---peace again.

1391
00:59:06,543 --> 00:59:08,512
Surprise is an excellent weapon.

1392
00:59:08,545 --> 00:59:09,680
-Hi Estelle.

1393
00:59:09,713 --> 00:59:10,648
How you doing, Mickey?

1394
00:59:10,682 --> 00:59:12,950
---intelligence, rather
than brute strength.

1395
00:59:12,983 --> 00:59:15,320
-Posture people.

1396
00:59:15,353 --> 00:59:16,753
Let;s snap it up a bit.

1397
00:59:16,787 --> 00:59:17,688
---they are stupid as well.

1398
00:59:17,722 --> 00:59:18,690
-(WHISPER) That's Gary.

1399
00:59:18,723 --> 00:59:20,725
---make frontal attacks
against their enemies.

1400
00:59:20,758 --> 00:59:21,960
They know you have
been pacified,

1401
00:59:21,993 --> 00:59:24,495
and won't be expecting
any resistance from you.

1402
00:59:24,528 --> 00:59:25,463
-Uh-huh.

1403
00:59:25,497 --> 00:59:27,065
-What we must do is
prepare a shock for them

1404
00:59:27,098 --> 00:59:30,100
when they arrive right
here, and then we'll

1405
00:59:30,133 --> 00:59:33,638
take them by surprise.

1406
00:59:33,672 --> 00:59:35,038
-The village is well situated.

1407
00:59:35,072 --> 00:59:37,108
-And so am I.

1408
00:59:37,142 --> 00:59:39,410
-Those rocks will act as
a wall to protect you.

1409
00:59:39,443 --> 00:59:40,278
-And vice versa.

1410
00:59:40,312 --> 00:59:42,013
-That side is
impassible to horses,

1411
00:59:42,047 --> 00:59:44,548
so they'll have to
attack from over there.

1412
00:59:44,582 --> 00:59:46,650
To fortify that
exposed side, I'll

1413
00:59:46,683 --> 00:59:49,020
need several sharp stakes,
ropes, and three men

1414
00:59:49,053 --> 00:59:50,588
to help me.

1415
00:59:50,622 --> 00:59:54,625
You, and you two, come with me.

1416
00:59:57,095 --> 00:59:58,028
Are you afraid?

1417
00:59:58,062 --> 00:59:59,930
-No.

1418
00:59:59,963 --> 01:00:01,498
-Won't you fight to
save your people?

1419
01:00:01,532 --> 01:00:02,100
-No.

1420
01:00:02,133 --> 01:00:03,433
But I will.

1421
01:00:03,467 --> 01:00:04,035
I want to fight.

1422
01:00:04,068 --> 01:00:05,537
-For my right to party!

1423
01:00:05,570 --> 01:00:06,103
-Good.

1424
01:00:06,137 --> 01:00:07,538
Who else will join him?

1425
01:00:07,572 --> 01:00:08,840
-All done back there?

1426
01:00:08,873 --> 01:00:11,008
---more of you here worthy
of being called men?

1427
01:00:11,042 --> 01:00:14,512
-Over here, Mr. Ator, yoo-hoo.

1428
01:00:14,545 --> 01:00:16,013
-Or are you no
better than sheep--

1429
01:00:16,047 --> 01:00:17,815
[bleating]

1430
01:00:17,848 --> 01:00:18,750
---not just [INAUDIBLE].

1431
01:00:18,783 --> 01:00:20,017
We are a people who--

1432
01:00:20,050 --> 01:00:21,152
-We need more Calgon.

1433
01:00:21,185 --> 01:00:22,087
---but you have convinced--

1434
01:00:22,120 --> 01:00:23,722
-My husband, some hot shot.

1435
01:00:23,755 --> 01:00:26,023
-Ancient Chinese secret, huh?

1436
01:00:28,727 --> 01:00:31,128
-Ator's prehistoric cave
dwellers and Milwaukee

1437
01:00:31,162 --> 01:00:34,665
are a long way apart, but they
have one thing in common-- cave

1438
01:00:34,698 --> 01:00:36,900
man means the best
human hears available,

1439
01:00:36,933 --> 01:00:40,237
and Milwaukee means sacred wine.

1440
01:00:40,270 --> 01:00:41,572
-Now Ator--

1441
01:00:41,605 --> 01:00:43,908
-Cream or sugar?

1442
01:00:43,942 --> 01:00:46,710
---first, let us
drink to your return.

1443
01:00:46,743 --> 01:00:48,980
And then we will
discuss your plan.

1444
01:00:49,013 --> 01:00:51,615
-Drink it all, sometimes
the poison's on the bottom.

1445
01:00:51,648 --> 01:00:53,050
---village of your ancestors.

1446
01:00:53,083 --> 01:00:53,617
May your stay--

1447
01:00:53,650 --> 01:00:55,620
-I've heard this part.

1448
01:00:55,653 --> 01:00:56,453
-Oh well.

1449
01:00:56,487 --> 01:00:58,857
-I thank you and
drink to the health,

1450
01:00:58,890 --> 01:01:00,023
prosperity, and liberty--

1451
01:01:00,057 --> 01:01:00,925
-Not bad.

1452
01:01:03,995 --> 01:01:06,030
-Champagne makes me giggly.

1453
01:01:06,063 --> 01:01:07,598
[Giggles]

1454
01:01:07,632 --> 01:01:09,633
-But let us organize ourselves--

1455
01:01:09,667 --> 01:01:10,935
-I smell a rat.

1456
01:01:10,968 --> 01:01:12,637
A big Commie rat.

1457
01:01:12,670 --> 01:01:15,507
-I'll need your strongest
men to build defenses.

1458
01:01:15,540 --> 01:01:17,007
-It's Timothy Leary!

1459
01:01:17,042 --> 01:01:19,110
I guess Liddy will have to
do the tour without him.

1460
01:01:19,143 --> 01:01:20,778
-Let's get to work.

1461
01:01:26,850 --> 01:01:28,085
-My name is Ravani.

1462
01:01:28,118 --> 01:01:32,557
Tell Ator they're
going to trap him.

1463
01:01:32,590 --> 01:01:34,592
-Yeah, yeah, get
some sleep, Quentin.

1464
01:01:34,625 --> 01:01:35,292
Ok?

1465
01:01:35,325 --> 01:01:36,793
Make sure you're drained good.

1466
01:01:36,827 --> 01:01:38,162
-Hello?

1467
01:01:38,195 --> 01:01:40,297
Your spit bucket's full.

1468
01:01:40,330 --> 01:01:44,235
OK, so, I'll just go now, OK?

1469
01:01:44,268 --> 01:01:46,837
Do I just leave the sign on
so the maid makes the room?

1470
01:01:46,870 --> 01:01:47,538
Ok.

1471
01:01:47,572 --> 01:01:51,275
[HUMMING] I'll close the door.

1472
01:01:57,782 --> 01:02:00,317
-Are you done with your
[MENACING LAUGH] drink?

1473
01:02:02,953 --> 01:02:06,790
-We secretly switched Ator's
coffee with Folger's Crystals.

1474
01:02:06,823 --> 01:02:07,725
Let's watch.

1475
01:02:13,865 --> 01:02:14,365
-He is huge.

1476
01:02:14,398 --> 01:02:15,567
-Timber!

1477
01:02:15,600 --> 01:02:19,837
-Oh, right, now we call this
film the Wong Dwellers, aww

1478
01:02:19,870 --> 01:02:20,370
yeah.

1479
01:02:20,403 --> 01:02:21,372
-Thong.

1480
01:02:21,405 --> 01:02:22,038
-Thong.

1481
01:02:22,072 --> 01:02:23,407
Yeah, Thong.

1482
01:02:23,440 --> 01:02:24,542
Sorry.

1483
01:02:24,575 --> 01:02:26,343
-Satellite picture shows
clouds coming in from the west,

1484
01:02:26,377 --> 01:02:29,247
but this should burn
off by about noon.

1485
01:02:29,280 --> 01:02:31,282
-Before the dawn of time.

1486
01:02:31,315 --> 01:02:32,350
A race of druids.

1487
01:02:32,383 --> 01:02:36,320
Nobody knew who they were
or where they came from.

1488
01:02:36,353 --> 01:02:37,122
-Cool.

1489
01:02:37,155 --> 01:02:39,323
-Boy, that cleared
up really quick.

1490
01:02:39,357 --> 01:02:41,058
-Yeah, I told you it would.

1491
01:02:44,095 --> 01:02:45,062
-We've been betrayed.

1492
01:02:45,095 --> 01:02:45,630
-Darn.

1493
01:02:45,663 --> 01:02:48,365
-But I'm still alive.

1494
01:02:48,398 --> 01:02:50,768
-Think so?

1495
01:02:50,802 --> 01:02:53,872
-I wonder if it wouldn't have
been easier if we had just

1496
01:02:53,905 --> 01:02:55,973
kept on going to the
aid of my father.

1497
01:02:56,007 --> 01:02:58,108
-Oh, Monday morning quarterback.

1498
01:02:58,142 --> 01:03:00,343
-No one's life is more
important than another's.

1499
01:03:00,377 --> 01:03:01,878
-Except mine.

1500
01:03:01,912 --> 01:03:03,915
-Your father would
have done the same.

1501
01:03:03,948 --> 01:03:05,182
-Wear a tiny leather bikini?

1502
01:03:08,585 --> 01:03:11,288
-This is CNN.

1503
01:03:11,322 --> 01:03:13,790
Luke.

1504
01:03:13,825 --> 01:03:16,327
-Check it out, they worship
the Munsingwear penguin.

1505
01:03:19,097 --> 01:03:21,365
-Now pardon us, did you
see a little tiny fox run

1506
01:03:21,398 --> 01:03:23,100
through here?

1507
01:03:23,133 --> 01:03:23,733
No?

1508
01:03:27,372 --> 01:03:29,040
-The village elder
was the one who

1509
01:03:29,073 --> 01:03:31,342
lured you to come to help us.

1510
01:03:31,375 --> 01:03:34,845
-In other words, those
two were part of the plan.

1511
01:03:34,878 --> 01:03:36,013
-I wish they were
part of the plot.

1512
01:03:36,047 --> 01:03:37,013
-Yes.

1513
01:03:37,047 --> 01:03:37,815
The others were against
it and wanted to fight,

1514
01:03:37,848 --> 01:03:40,183
but the majority
were too terrified.

1515
01:03:40,217 --> 01:03:42,487
The elder's going to hand
you over to the Kungs.

1516
01:03:42,520 --> 01:03:45,288
In exchange, they've promised
to stop killing our people.

1517
01:03:45,322 --> 01:03:46,390
-All right, who's talking?

1518
01:03:46,423 --> 01:03:47,358
-I can't figure it out.

1519
01:03:47,392 --> 01:03:48,325
-Must be the director.

1520
01:03:48,358 --> 01:03:50,895
---allied with Zor.

1521
01:03:50,928 --> 01:03:52,497
-And what happened to Ravani?

1522
01:03:52,530 --> 01:03:54,565
-The new elder has been
slowly poisoning him

1523
01:03:54,598 --> 01:03:57,000
because he knew Ravani
would warn you if he could.

1524
01:03:57,033 --> 01:03:57,835
-Fun.

1525
01:03:57,868 --> 01:04:00,037
-I think Ravani
must be dead by now.

1526
01:04:00,070 --> 01:04:01,038
[Yelling]

1527
01:04:01,072 --> 01:04:02,940
-Hey, it's Teddy Roosevelt
and Rough Riders!

1528
01:04:02,973 --> 01:04:04,842
-I think it's the Kurds.

1529
01:04:04,875 --> 01:04:06,077
-And whey?

1530
01:04:06,110 --> 01:04:06,910
-Yes whey.

1531
01:04:06,943 --> 01:04:08,378
-They are terrifying,
aren't they?

1532
01:04:08,412 --> 01:04:10,247
With those bandanas,
and they all

1533
01:04:10,280 --> 01:04:13,817
look very Machiavellian
with their shirts off.

1534
01:04:13,850 --> 01:04:14,252
-Machiavellian?

1535
01:04:18,555 --> 01:04:19,357
-Hiya Phil.

1536
01:04:19,390 --> 01:04:20,457
-Morning, Tom.

1537
01:04:20,490 --> 01:04:23,360
-A month has now
passed, old one.

1538
01:04:23,393 --> 01:04:25,195
Have you done what you said?

1539
01:04:25,228 --> 01:04:26,963
-[INAUDIBLE] we have
kept our promise.

1540
01:04:26,997 --> 01:04:29,867
Now you must keep yours.

1541
01:04:29,900 --> 01:04:33,037
I give you Ator, but
in return, our village

1542
01:04:33,070 --> 01:04:37,342
will no longer have to
sacrifice to your serpent god.

1543
01:04:37,375 --> 01:04:39,510
-Uh, that must mean no.

1544
01:04:39,543 --> 01:04:41,078
-No, I think so.

1545
01:04:41,112 --> 01:04:43,413
[Shouting]

1546
01:04:43,447 --> 01:04:44,048
-Grr!

1547
01:04:47,217 --> 01:04:47,618
-Yee-hoo!

1548
01:04:50,955 --> 01:04:54,692
-Those are the Pillage People.

1549
01:04:54,725 --> 01:04:55,392
-No!

1550
01:04:55,425 --> 01:04:57,027
-No.

1551
01:04:57,060 --> 01:05:01,065
-That's not fair, I'm the
star of the show. [SOB]

1552
01:05:12,208 --> 01:05:13,710
-Oh duh, I'm sure.

1553
01:05:13,743 --> 01:05:15,312
My hair is getting singed.

1554
01:05:15,345 --> 01:05:18,715
Last time I go club
hopping with this guy.

1555
01:05:18,748 --> 01:05:20,383
-Honey, start
lighting those huts!

1556
01:05:23,753 --> 01:05:26,590
-A job well done.

1557
01:05:26,623 --> 01:05:28,225
-No!

1558
01:05:28,258 --> 01:05:29,627
No!

1559
01:05:29,660 --> 01:05:30,260
Please.

1560
01:05:34,232 --> 01:05:35,767
-Looks like back
lot at Universal.

1561
01:05:35,800 --> 01:05:38,168
[Gasping]

1562
01:05:38,202 --> 01:05:41,472
-Feel the burn, come
on, go for the burn.

1563
01:05:41,505 --> 01:05:43,473
-Hey, here's just a wild
idea, why don't you rotate

1564
01:05:43,507 --> 01:05:46,110
to the other side of the
pole where the fire isn't?

1565
01:05:46,143 --> 01:05:48,678
-This scene brought you
by Kingsford Charcoal.

1566
01:05:48,712 --> 01:05:50,682
-Edges light quickly.

1567
01:05:50,715 --> 01:05:53,283
-You know, they shouldn't have
filmed this at Yellowstone.

1568
01:05:53,317 --> 01:05:54,652
-Yay!

1569
01:05:54,685 --> 01:05:55,585
